Privacy Policy for Bible Quotes

Last Updated: 25/02/2025
Thank you for using Bible Quotes. Your privacy is important to us, and we are committed to protecting it. This Privacy Policy explains how we handle information in connection with your use of our Chrome extension.

1. Data Collection
Bible Quotes does not collect, store, or share any personal or sensitive user data. We do not track your activities, and we do not require any permissions that would allow us to access your personal information.

2. Permissions
Bible Quotes may request certain permissions to function properly, such as storage access. These permissions are used solely for the functionality of the extension and are not used to collect or transmit any data.

3. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date. We encourage you to review this Privacy Policy periodically to stay informed about how we are protecting your information.

4. Local Analytics (Optional)
Bible Quotes stores minimal, non-personal usage events locally in your browser to compute in-extension analytics such as most-saved verses, theme distributions, and short-term trends. Examples of stored events: action type (show, favorite, unfavorite, share), quote text or reference, and a timestamp. These events are stored only in your browser's local storage and are not transmitted to any external server.

You can opt out at any time from the extension Options page; opting out will stop new events from being recorded. When you opt out you may choose to clear previously collected analytics data from the Options page — this permanently removes locally stored events. Events are retained only for a limited period (default: 90 days) and older events are automatically trimmed to a reasonable maximum size. No analytics data is transmitted off your device.

4. Contact Us
If you have any questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at carlosluquetrad@gmail.com
